\title{Batching and Grinding}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Two engineering devices that materially change the security accounting, and are therefore easy to get wrong.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Batched FRI: many words, one folding argument. What the random combination costs in soundness, and what ArkLib's \code{BatchedFri} states.}
        \li{Batching across constraint polynomials in a STARK, and how it interacts with [DEEP](dhsorens-0039).}
        \li{[Proof-of-work grinding](dhsorens-004E): converting prover hash work into verifier confidence, and the exact form of the resulting bound.}
        \li{How many bits of a deployed security level come from grinding rather than from the protocol.}
        \li{Whether grinding is accounted for in the [round-by-round](dhsorens-002F) analysis or bolted on afterwards.}
    }
}
